Local LLMs vs API-based LLMs


| Aspect             |   Local LLMs** (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp)                          | API-based LLMs** (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Vertex AI)                                 |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
|   Setup            | Need to download model weights & runtime (may require GPU/strong CPU). | Just need an API key, no setup on your machine.                                          |
|   Cost             | Free after setup (no per-token charges, only hardware/electricity).    | Pay per token or per API call; costs increase with usage.                                |
| Data Privacy       | 100% private; prompts & data stay on your system.                      | Data leaves your environment (unless provider offers private deployment).                |
| Model Size         | Usually smaller (3B–13B parameters, some 70B but heavy).               | Access to latest & largest models (e.g., GPT-4, Claude 3, Gemini Pro, 1M token context). |
| Performance        | Depends on your hardware (GPU/CPU/RAM). Can be slower on big models.   | Optimized in the cloud with GPUs/TPUs; generally faster for large tasks.                 |
| Scalability        | Limited to your machine’s resources. Hard to serve many users.         | Scales automatically; can handle millions of requests.                                   |
| Customization      | Full control — fine-tuning, quantization, offline use.                 | Limited customization; fine-tuning allowed but controlled by provider.                   |
| Context Window     | Smaller (4k–16k tokens in most local models).                          | Very large (100k–1M tokens in modern APIs).                                              |
| Maintenance        | You must update models & manage environment.                           | Provider handles updates, hosting, scaling, optimizations.                               |
| Offline Use        |  Works without internet once model is downloaded.                      | Requires internet & provider’s servers.                                                |
